.git
.github
.claude
docs
*.md
.env
data

# Runtime data of the Synology NAS variant (docker-compose.nas.yml) lives in
# bind-mounted folders inside the clone. Without these lines the build context
# would contain the live Postgres data directory: files owned by the postgres
# user that the context reader cannot always read (the build fails), a copy of
# the database in every `COPY . .` layer, and gigabytes sent to the daemon on
# every build. Patterns match at the context root only, so internal/uploads is
# not excluded.
pgdata
uploads
imagecache
ts_inventory_state

# Backup archives (docs/specs/15-backup-restore-and-export.md) land in ./backups
# in the clone. Without this line every `docker compose build` would ship the
# whole backup history into the build context - gigabytes, growing.
backups

# The E2E harness and its runtime artifacts never belong in the application
# image: it is a separate, throwaway test container, not something the
# Dockerfile builds or ships (docs/specs/05-frontend-pwa-foundations.md).
# node_modules in particular has broken this build before — npm's symlinks,
# written through the e2e/ bind mount, are not something Docker's tar-based
# build context reader tolerates.
e2e/
